# __PROJECT_NAME__

A [Maximus](https://github.com/getarbol/maximus) service on Cloudflare Workers. It
declares each operation once and serves it over HTTP with its OpenAPI document, and, when an
operation asks for them, as an MCP tool and a Worker RPC method.

## Before the first deployment

`src/app.ts` uses placeholders: set `origin` to the service's public HTTPS origin, `tokens.audience`
to the audience its access tokens carry and `tokens.issuer` to the authorization server that issues
them. The starter declares no operation, so it serves only its discovery documents and `/health`.

## Run it locally

`bun run dev` serves the Worker on `localhost` with `cf dev`. `maximus init` wrote a random development
token to `.dev.vars`, which Git ignores and `cloudflare.config.ts` declares for `cf dev` alone, so no
deployed build carries it. From `localhost` it is a developer holding every scope the service declares:

```sh
TOKEN=$(sed 's/^DEVELOPMENT_TOKEN=//' .dev.vars)
curl -H "authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" http://localhost:5173/v1/<your operation's route>
```

## Commands

| Command                         | Runs                                                                                         |
| ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `bun install`                   | Installs the dependencies.                                                                   |
| `bun run dev`                   | The Worker locally, with `cf dev`.                                                           |
| `bun run typecheck`             | Generates the binding and runtime types with `cf workers types`, then TypeScript.            |
| `bun run check` / `bun run fix` | Lint and format with the Maximus presets.                                                    |
| `bun run test`                  | The tests, in the Workers runtime.                                                           |
| `bun run build`                 | `cf build`, which writes the build `cf deploy` uploads.                                      |
| `bun run verify`                | Everything above.                                                                            |
| `bun run deploy`                | `verify`, then deploys that same build with `cf deploy`. Sign in with `cf auth login` first. |

## Layout

- `src/app.ts`: the application. Declare operations in resource modules
  (`src/api/<resource>/operations.ts`) that build on `base`, and mount each module here once.
- `src/index.ts`: the Worker: its default export serves HTTP, and the named entrypoint serves RPC.
- `tests/`: the contract smoke and the tests for what is specific to this service.

Use synthetic data in tests, give previews their own resources and never point CI at production.
Keep credentials and provider evidence out of the repository (`.private/` is ignored).
